      "x": 0,
      "y": 1240,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "Reading PDFs and photos (planned)\n\nDrop PDFs or photos → each is read a page at a time by the Ollama model picked in Settings → a finished report waits for review → Save report files it under the matching patient.\n\nNothing leaves this computer, and uploaded files are deleted after reading. Mock data only."
    },
    {
      "id": "why-timeline",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 640,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "B · Report timeline\nWhy: matches how results arrive, one report at a time, and makes each report's flags obvious.\nTradeoff: trends need a click into a test; comparing two tests means switching back and forth."
    },
    {
      "id": "why-table",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 840,
      "y": 640,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "C · Results table\nWhy: every value for every date on one screen; the fastest to scan.\nTradeoff: no room for reference bands or axes; feels clinical and dense for anyone who isn't used to lab reports."
    }
  ],
